# システム環境設定's tags pulled out (docs/tessronos 10.6, 11.6): a tag pressed and moved further
# than LK_DRAG_W is pulled out (OB_E_PULL) rather than chosen, its outline is carried by the desktop
# (DT_RQ_CARRY), and where it is let go the object of its page, named システム環境設定：背景, is made
# and a link to it put (DT_RQ_PLACE, lib/libtv/tv_page.c). For tools/x64/ui_run64.py with the image of make TARGET=_X64_ DESKTOP=1 UITEST=1
# sdimg a KTEST=1 build. The window is at 160,80, opened on 〈画面〉〈配色〉; 〈背景〉 is
# the first tag of the lower row, at 192,151. BTRON, the first window, shows left of it at 100,200.
openapp 01a0d8c4-52b6-7b52-9d72-3e8fa01b2c42 {"tessronos-sysenv":{"data":"colour"}}
expect sysenv: page "colour"
expect sysenv: ready
wait 800
move 900 700
wait 300
shot stp_before
# 〈背景〉 pressed, moved past LK_DRAG_W on the tag, carried into BTRON and let go there
logmark
move 192 151
down
move 197 152
expectsince tvpage: tag 3 pulled out, page "wallpaper", outline
move 170 170
wait 300
move 130 190
wait 300
move 100 200
wait 500
up
expectsince sysenv: link of page "wallpaper" carried (0)
expectsince tvpage: object "システム環境設定：背景" of page "wallpaper" made (0)
expectsince tvpage: link of page "wallpaper" carried, named "システム環境設定：背景" (0)
expectsince cabinet: dropped 1
wait 800
shot stp_put
# the link put shows the name of the page's object, システム環境設定：背景, whole in its band (the
# letters right of the pointer, recorded from a run that put it)
shotsum stp_put 128 191 262 205
want ok 32902fa4cc82fbcd
# the page shown stays 〈配色〉: the tag was not chosen
absent sysenv: page "wallpaper"
shotsame stp_before stp_put 180 230 730 560
# the link put opened as a double press opens it: the page of its applist in the same window
logmark
dclick 100 200
expectsince sysenv: opened with data "wallpaper"
expectsince sysenv: page "wallpaper"
wait 500
shot stp_open
nwin システム環境設定
want ok 1
# a press let go on the tag without moving still chooses it, and carries nothing
logmark
click 235 151
wait 500
absent sysenv: tag 4 pulled out
shot stp_click
absent !OACV!
